      "message": "I actually think we could probably use the other helper that we use for shader modules, i.e. here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp;l\u003d2209;drc\u003d746b6b8836d1f832ade517ba09d5149cbb58ec3f;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1 instead since I suspect we will never really want to allow multiple entry types. \n\nExample:\n```\nif (!unpacked.Empty()) {\n    [[maybe_unused]] wgpu::SType type;\n    DAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(\n      type,\n      (unpacked.ValidateBranches\u003c\n          Branch\u003cTexelBufferBindingEntry\u003e,\n          Branch\u003cExternalTextureBindingEntry\u003e\u003e()));\n}\n```\n\nIt\u0027s a bit unfortunate that we need the not-empty clause atm because I don\u0027t think that helper allows no extensions atm. But this will be useful in the sense that it catches that there\u0027s is at most 1 valid extension in case we add more types in the future.",
